  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 112,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Fever · headache · stiff neck · altered mental status: think MENINGITIS",
   "lines": [
    "classic triad: FEVER, ALTERED MENTAL STATUS, NUCHAL RIGIDITY (Kernig's, Brudzinski's)",
    "language trouble, confusion, focal seizures → think ENCEPHALITIS (the brain itself)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 138,
   "w": 894,
   "h": 42,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "Suspected CNS infection: treat FIRST, then let the CSF decide",
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "id": "p",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 220,
   "w": 894,
   "h": 132,
   "kind": "info",
   "title": "Plan",
   "lines": [
    "1 · CULTURE a blood sample",
    "2 · START EMPIRIC treatment now: never wait for the CT or the tap",
    "3 · CT/MRI FIRST only if focal signs or ↓ consciousness (PUNISH: Papilledema, Unconscious, Neurologic deficit, Immunocompromised, Seizure, History of CNS disease) → mass = NEUROSURGERY",
    "4 · LUMBAR PUNCTURE → adjust treatment to the CSF"
   ]
  },
